From 0adc69d3cd652527a3203f6e830b4348df79bf10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:26:09 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(contour)!: climb milling runs climb - outside
 clockwise, inside counter-clockwise with M3

With a right-hand (M3) spindle, climb milling keeps the material on the
RIGHT of the tool's travel: an outside profile runs clockwise, an inside
profile counter-clockwise, and control compensation is G41. The 2D
Contour family called "material on the left" climb, so every contour
posted with the default climb flag was conventional-milled.

- contour: ring travel follows `climb == inside`; the air side (leads,
  fillets, arc entries) and G41/G42 follow the corrected travel; the
  comp room's arc law reads the tool side from the travel.
- each ring keeps its seam; climb and conventional differ only in
  direction (ring::walked).
- a keep-down ring-to-ring link is proved against both rings' leads too.
- the open-boundary contour hands its run on material-right.
- 2D Chamfer takes the side: boss edge CW, bore edge CCW under climb.
- cl: a vertical arc's Z-extremum split at an off-lattice end no longer
  leaves a sub-micron sliver.
- 2D Pocket wall pass already ran climb: pinned, not changed.

BREAKING CHANGE: posted G-code of every 2D Contour and 2D Chamfer
reverses direction (G41/G42 swap under control/wear compensation); a
project that set climb: false as a workaround now posts conventional.

Fixes #1555

